---
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
---

<section class="section problem">
  <div class="container--narrow">
    <SectionHeader>
      You have funding and a thesis.<br />
      <span class="text-accent">Now what?</span>
    </SectionHeader>
    <div data-fade data-fade-delay="0.1">
      <p class="text-body-lg problem__text">
        You're not technical, and every engineer you talk to gives you a different
        answer about what to build, how long it'll take, and what it should cost.
        You can't evaluate their answers. You don't know which corners are safe to
        cut and which ones will cost you six months later. The longer you spend
        figuring this out, the more runway you burn and the wider your market
        window opens for someone else.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div data-fade data-fade-delay="0.12">
      <p class="text-body-lg problem__text">
        Maybe you've tried vibe coding a prototype yourself. It works until it
        doesn't. No auth, no error handling, no infrastructure, no security. You
        end up with a demo that can't become a product and a codebase that has to
        be thrown away.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div data-fade data-fade-delay="0.2">
      <p class="text-body-lg problem__text">
        You don't need a bigger team. You don't need another vendor who disappears
        after launch. You need a team that's been on both sides of that table.
        Who's been the CTO at an early-stage company, built products from scratch,
        and knows exactly what it takes to get something real into the market.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div data-fade data-fade-delay="0.25">
      <p class="text-body-lg problem__closer">That's what we do.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem__text {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .problem__closer {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
</style>
